            <ArticleTitle>Assessment of a patient with orofacial pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>57-60</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pain is the commonest complaint that brings a patient to a dentist. Most pain is acute, rapidly diagnosed and managed. However, more chronic pain must be more carefully evaluated if it is to be managed successfully. This paper proposes a systematic approach to the taking of a pain history and gives a short differential diagnosis of facial pain of non-dental origin.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
